financebench_id_01865,"If we exclude the impact of M&A, which segment has dragged down 3M's overall growth in 2022?",The consumer segment shrunk by 0.9% organically.,3M_2022_10K,novel-generated,"In 2022, the segment that dragged down 3M's overall growth, excluding the impact of mergers and acquisitions (M&A), was primarily the **Health Care** segment. This was attributed to various factors including declines in certain product categories, particularly in the separation and purification and health information systems areas, which faced challenges due to post-COVID demand normalization and hospital budget constraints. Additionally, the overall operational challenges coupled with litigation costs also impacted earnings, with significant charges related to ongoing legal matters and other impairments being reported ([3M 2022 10-K](data/pdf/3M_2022_10K.pdf)). 

The Consumer segment, while affected by broader economic factors, did not seem to have as significant of a negative impact on overall growth as the Health Care segment did when considering organic growth metrics and excluding M&A ([3M 2022 10-K](data/pdf/3M_2022_10K.pdf)).",,,"[""3M_2022_10K"", ""3M_2018_10K"", ""3M_2023Q2_10Q""]","Source: data\pdfs\3M_2022_10K.pdf

